     "text": "Martinez PLC Medical Group\nRe: Christine Taylor (DOB 03/14/2007)\n\nDr. Randy Blackburn\nNeurologist\n\nFebruary 7, 2025\n\nTo Whom It May Concern,\n\nI am writing to provide a comprehensive medical summary of my patient, Christine Taylor, who was seen on February 7, 2025, regarding her transient ischemic attack (TIA). Her blood pressure was recorded at 121/83, and she weighed 199 pounds at the time of her visit. Christine has a history TIA that began approximately I.3 years ago, and she has been under continuous monitoring since then.\n\nDuring today's visit, Christine reported no recent episodes of TIA symptoms. Her neurologic examination was normal with no focal deficits, and cranial nerves II through XII were intact. Her reflexes were symmetrical, and she exhibited no signs of dysarthria or ataxia. Additionally, a review of her systems revealed no new complaints. She continues to be on a medication regimen as needed, but no specific anticoagulant or antiplatelet therapy is currently prescribed.\n\nChristine's blood pressure has remained within a stable range over her recent visits, and her weight has been relatively consistent. Her blood pressure readings and weights from past few visits are as follows:\n- September 21, 2024: Blood pressure 125/84, weight 200 pounds.\n- May 4, 2024: Blood pressure 120/80, weight 186 pounds.\n- December 17, 2023: Blood pressure 132/84, weight 197 pounds.\n- July 30, 2023: Blood pressure 126/84, weight 188 pounds.\n- March 12, 2023: Blood pressure 121/80, weight 199 pounds.\n- October 24, 2022: Blood pressure 127/83, weight 190 pounds.\n- June 6, 2022: Blood pressure 128/89, weight pounds.\n- January 17, 2022: Blood pressure 120/90, weight 187 pounds.\n\nChristine has been compliant with her follow-ups and has not reported any new or worsening symptoms related to her TIA. In the interim, she has also seen her primary care physician for various other issues, such as a back strain and an upper respiratory infection (URI). She has shown resilience and a positive attitude towards her ongoing health management.\n\nAdditionally, it is important to note that Christine has a history of tobacco use. She was a former cigarette smoker, having smoked approximately 1.5 cigarettes per day, and she quit smoking in June 2018. Her disclosure about her smoking has been honest and consistent.\n\nChristine's family history includes type 2 diabetes in her mother, who was diagnosed at the age of 80, although the status of her mother's current health is not known as she passed away at an unknown you for considering this detailed account"
